        "date": "2026-05-30T10:27:55Z"
      },
      "message": "Fail over on 404 from always-present Esplora paths\n\nmempool.space serves a 404 (instead of 429) to rate-limited clients,\nwhich is common on carrier-NAT'd mobile connections where many users\nshare an egress IP. esploraFetch treated 404 as a legitimate \"not\nfound\", marked the endpoint healthy, and returned it WITHOUT failing\nover — so getFeeRates threw 'Failed to fetch fee estimates', the query\nswallowed it, and the Send dialog showed no fee rates. This is why fees\nloaded on WiFi but not LTE.\n\nAdd a per-call retryStatuses option to esploraFetch that extends the\nretryable set (failover + cool-down) for that call, and apply [404] to\nthe paths that always exist on a healthy backend: /fee-estimates,\n/address, /address/txs, /address/utxo, and the /tx broadcast. The\n/tx/{txid} lookup keeps 404 meaningful (genuinely-unknown tx).\n\nRegression-of: 406371af",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "79c4b7cabf6a2ac7ac78e15a0002e3cb90fe43ce",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/trees/79c4b7cabf6a2ac7ac78e15a0002e3cb90fe43ce"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/commits/f8f51f2e0ccd190f71fabe822c76fabb79f2a5c2",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEESof9JJzQIzN3kpf4chHR+ZdE+7cFAmoau6sACgkQchHR+ZdE\n+7fpdA/7BHJbKeHZ8Cmhpm5bQl4HDvQYsFBdIghymdIZJpuxGvMyflFFAbisJkmg\nLZIg+DQs+sOdn/bi/gLSjXEeCTvqUfRrA79AjOazFdkPfAd8HUMdHbXnPglZiKOr\nPC/223/554hANJDXOoplfVLcawzowOkURoHOu8YpEkgz7Kt3x6/behSKsesEouy4\nuxVbF2TaXMLvfPF6xrjaDz3zuXNSdag3bN++s2ISFQfDKMhwX/wqRfm5qyR0eXmj\n7oylEFKNrBtdAIeuxLvjwa8vg5x1qTO+IcDOsFmSgh071iq1X88CHBsFjikRPqxa\nrNyzt6FIIF7cNPy8MsBYSL4fKWCaRMbTsBq3L8/ugVuPfEWGc4OZ+aLwQhCBEnlF\nGE2fRscz+kH4HXO6MBCEp92NOVk7DNtwEeQ//IrknUHm8dmXYfcVhGv0J3jeCwEA\nxNse8LqDZamnBYXPOxDMCtdYzdL8gnmEx1N2mpmZ+Sz1+64G00N43/1q8UWn3HZW\nbyMbkj0zBYm0MatN12jVRHVwB+GQ0P8qZtJz5TuV/yjekxkGa+iyh47tx39ZWa2B\nRtVktJW/Ouz0Ojd5jrw2DIgUxi4GQOSYhRcvLIULHZcTYCPu5a29N49vsHaFYq8C\nJFd7BJlsIHtio1nJpcKGzDNOe+imDk4GhX3wF154kkryxyjaM/I=\n=Plop\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----",
        "payload": "tree 79c4b7cabf6a2ac7ac78e15a0002e3cb90fe43ce\nparent 55d92aa9f4d0ec78e8bfadcf93b18f313aa0cbf2\nauthor Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1780136864 +0200\ncommitter Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1780136875 +0200\n\nFail over on 404 from always-present Esplora paths\n\nmempool.space serves a 404 (instead of 429) to rate-limited clients,\nwhich is common on carrier-NAT'd mobile connections where many users\nshare an egress IP. esploraFetch treated 404 as a legitimate \"not\nfound\", marked the endpoint healthy, and returned it WITHOUT failing\nover — so getFeeRates threw 'Failed to fetch fee estimates', the query\nswallowed it, and the Send dialog showed no fee rates. This is why fees\nloaded on WiFi but not LTE.\n\nAdd a per-call retryStatuses option to esploraFetch that extends the\nretryable set (failover + cool-down) for that call, and apply [404] to\nthe paths that always exist on a healthy backend: /fee-estimates,\n/address, /address/txs, /address/utxo, and the /tx broadcast. The\n/tx/{txid} lookup keeps 404 meaningful (genuinely-unknown tx).\n\nRegression-of: 406371af\n",
